WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.501
A bit about Carnegie Mellon.

2
00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:06.106
We are a private research university
with about 14,800 students,

3
00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:11.106
7,300 of which are undergraduates,
and 7,400 of which are graduate students.

4
00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.545
Amongst the undergrads,

5
00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:15.515
50% are male, 47% are female,

6
00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.851
and about 3% are nonbinary.

7
00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:21.287
As you can probably tell, we are in
Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, which is known

8
00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:25.158
as the City of Bridges, and we are located
roughly five miles from downtown.

9
00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:28.161
Today, we will show
you eight undergraduate colleges.

10
00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.763
We have one graduate only school,

11
00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:33.400
which is the Heinz College of
Information Systems and Public Policy,

12
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.769
which is situated right outside on Forbes Avenue.

13
00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.071
But we will not be visiting that today.

14
00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:43.071
Carnegie Mellon was founded in the year
1900 by Andrew Carnegie and merged in 1967

15
00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.712
with the Mellon Institute
of Industrial Research,

16
00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.380
which was founded by Andrew Mellon.

17
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.283
And they became CMU, as you know it today.

18
00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:53.186
Both of our founders are named Andrew,
and coincidentally,

19
00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.055
they also share the same Scottish heritage.

20
00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:57.724
So our mascot is Scotty,
the Scottish Terrier,

21
00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.225
and our color is the tartan plaid,

22
00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:02.429
which is a nod
to our traditional Scottish heritage.

23
00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.365
We'll introduce
more of that today on tour.

24
00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.901
And one of our biggest traditions on
campus is Buggy,

25
00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.003
which you can see
on the welcome center wall.

26
00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.572
And it's sort of like
a five-legged relay race.

27
00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.008
Our first stop is going to be
the Tepper School of Business.

